      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Mainstream climate policy often treats the phase-out as a non-negotiable baseline because the scientific consensus indicates that even moderate policy delays could permanently lock into irreversible temperature increases. Proponents argue that climate tipping points and existential risks to humanity create an ethical imperative that supersedes all other systemic concerns. However, critics and your research correctly identify that framing equity as merely a \"side problem\" ignores the political reality that unjust transitions can weaken the very international alliances needed to enforce them.",
